From 0f9919e2008996041419a124b54db0f6c71a43d5 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: so1_sanctum <so1_sanctum@pm.me>
Date: Wed, 7 Oct 2026 23:43:31 -0400
Subject: [PATCH 1/2] ptlc: embedded contract API, BIP-340 and secp256k1
 helpers, adaptor signatures

Definitions.ptlc and PtlcApi mirror the htlc ones for the ptlc contract of
go-zenon branch ptlc/release-0.0.9 (Create with a destination, Unlock,
ProxyUnlock, Reclaim, getById, and the domain-separated unlock message).
Secp256k1 and Bip340 are built on pointycastle's curve, which the SDK
already depends on: BIP-340 signing and verification pass the official
vectors; the single-signer adaptor construction is tested in all four key
and nonce parity cases and cross-checked by the Go side of zenon-ptlc.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.1 <noreply@anthropic.com>
